The analyzed Gremlin variant uploads a ZIP of stolen data, named with the victim's public IP address, to an attacker-controlled web panel, with the Telegram Bot API as an alternative path, rather than using HTTPS POST with Telegram as a secondary channel. Its clipper swaps any copied cryptocurrency wallet address matching its patterns, not only Bitcoin and Ethereum addresses, and Unit 42 does not list saved passwords among the stolen data. The session-hijack module requests session data from the running Chromium browser process over WebSocket, and one sample is protected by a commercial packer with instruction virtualization.
